Campfire wasm patch 0112: the engine refuses invoke data that raises its app's privilege (issue #73).

process_invoke_data takes invoke data back from the client. When the data carries an app
invocation to re-run later (Flags::SaveAppInvoke, written for dependent calls),
contract_transaction.cpp re-runs that app body at vData.m_AppInvoke.m_Privilege, a value the
client wrote (BuildTxOnce, RebuildHft: aex.set_Privilege). At privilege 1 an app body derives
keys from the master KDF (get_PkEx, get_BlindSk, SetKernelAdv without a foreign signature): the
keys BEAM names and every other dApp use. Stock ShadersManager::ProcessTxData starts the
transaction whatever privilege the data names. Core patch 0002 refuses this for wallet-api
(PrivilegeRoutingShadersManager::ProcessTxData in api_cli.cpp); the wasm client's app APIs
(WasmWalletClient.createAppAPI -> WalletClient::IWThread_createAppShaders) use the stock
ShadersManager, so the web wallet was protected only by its JavaScript
(pwa/src/lib/dapps/policy.js checkContractData).

With this, ShadersManager::ProcessTxData refuses invoke data whose app privilege is above 0
unless
  - it is not above the privilege of the manager processing it (the app API's own, chosen at
    createAppAPI), and
  - the app body is one this manager compiled itself at that privilege (SHA-256 of the
    compiled body, recorded in compileAppShader), as 0002 accepts only bodies wallet-api
    compiled from an allowlisted shader.
The refusal goes back as the API's ContractError (-32019, "Contract call failed") with
error.data "invoke data requests a shader privilege that was not granted (<why>)", which
starts with the text wallet-api's 0002 sends; no transaction is created. Invoke data at
privilege 0, and invoke data a manager produced itself (invoke_contract), are unaffected.
The check runs where 0002's does, after the client's consent handler: the page's own
check (policy.js) still refuses such data first, before anyone is asked.

wasm tree only: in wallet-api, 0002 hands accepted privileged data to a privilege-0 stock
manager, which this check would then refuse.

